description: Do not reference functional requirements (RF) IDs in code comments or docstrings
globs: apps/**/*.{py,ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: true
---

# No RF references in application code

- Do **not** put functional-requirements IDs or section references (e.g. `RF-1`, `RF-3.6.2`, “requisitos funcionales”) in Python/TypeScript **comments**, **module docstrings**, or **inline documentation** under `apps/`.
- Product requirements live in `docs/requisitos-funcionales-luneta.md`; code should describe **behavior** in plain language, not traceability IDs.
- **Tests** may describe behavior in plain English in module docstrings; still avoid `RF-x` tags.
- Planning in chat or markdown docs outside `apps/` may reference RFs when useful for the user.
